---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/docs/Tag.astro";
import { DOC_GROUPS } from "../../components/docs/nav";
import { REPO_URL, ISSUES_URL } from "../../data/site";

const groups = DOC_GROUPS.map((g) => ({ ...g, pages: g.pages.filter((p) => p.path !== "/docs") })).filter((g) => g.pages.length);
---

<DocsLayout>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Pre-alpha.</strong> Install it with <code>curl -fsSL https://coding.sh/install | sh</code>. Every command, flag and file format can still change. This page lists what exists in the code today and what is only planned.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what">What it is</h2>
  <p>
    coding.sh is open-source, local-first observability and evals for AI agents. Think of a local LangSmith, Braintrust or
    Judgment Labs: traces and evals stay on your disk, in one npm package with zero runtime dependencies, on Node 22.15 or newer.
  </p>
  <p>
    It works with any agent. Your own agent, built on the OpenAI Agents SDK, LangGraph, the Vercel AI SDK, the Claude Agent SDK or plain
    code, sends traces over OpenTelemetry or the TypeScript and Python SDKs. Coding agents are first-class: adapters capture prompts, tool
    calls, model calls, file changes and subagents from Claude Code, Codex and ten other agents with no code changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="start">Start here</h2>
  <div class="doc-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>You have</th><th>Start with</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Your own agent or LLM app</td><td><a href="/docs/how-to/trace-your-agent">Trace your own agent</a>: OpenTelemetry or the SDK, then evals on those runs.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and others)</td><td><a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a>: one install line adds the hooks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>An app in production</td><td><a href="/docs/production">Production</a>: <code>coding.sh serve</code> on SQLite or Postgres.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>New to the terms? Read <a href="/docs/concepts">Concepts</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="status">What is built</h2>
  <div class="doc-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Area</th><th>Status</th><th>What exists</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Coding-agent capture</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td>Hook, plugin and extension adapters for 11 agents, and a wrapper for Aider and any other command. <a href="/docs/agents">Matrix</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>OTLP receiver</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td><code>coding.sh collector</code> on 127.0.0.1:4318: OTLP/HTTP, JSON or protobuf, GenAI, OpenInference and AI SDK attributes. <a href="/docs/otel">Setup</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>TypeScript and Python SDKs</td>
          <td><Tag status="partial" /></td>
          <td>Wrap OpenAI and Anthropic clients, trace turns and tool calls, AI SDK tracer. In the repository, not on npm or PyPI yet. <a href="/docs/sdk">Reference</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Explore</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td><code>sessions</code>, <code>show</code>, <code>search</code> (SQLite FTS5) and a local viewer, <code>coding.sh ui</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Datasets and experiments</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td>Versioned datasets, nine deterministic grader kinds plus LLM judges, paired comparison with a bootstrap CI and McNemar's test. <a href="/docs/evals">Evals</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Judge calibration</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td>Cohen's κ against human labels on a held-out split; uncalibrated judges are flagged.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Repo-replay tasks</td>
          <td><Tag status="partial" /></td>
          <td>Task drafting, verifier validation, harness bundles and A/B compare exist. Sessions recorded with <code>coding.sh run --</code> carry repo snapshots and can become tasks; hook-captured sessions can't yet. <a href="/docs/evals#repo-replay">Details</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Storage and sinks</td>
          <td><Tag status="built" /></td>
          <td>SQLite index, zstd blob store, OTLP and HTTP sinks, plugin loading for other stores. <a href="/docs/storage">Storage</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Postgres, S3 stores</td>
          <td><Tag status="partial" /></td>
          <td>Plugin packages in the repository, used by <code>coding.sh serve</code>. Not on npm yet. <a href="/docs/production">Production</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tool evals</td>
          <td><Tag status="planned" /></td>
          <td>A design spec for scoring how well agents use a CLI, MCP server or API. <a href="/docs/tool-evals">Spec</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>npm package</td>
          <td><Tag status="planned" /></td>
          <td>The name is reserved in <code>package.json</code>; nothing is published.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="how">How it fits together</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Capture.</strong> Your own agent sends OpenTelemetry spans to <code>coding.sh collector</code>, or SDK events to <code>coding.sh serve</code>. A coding agent's hook runs <code>~/.coding.sh/bin/hook.mjs</code>, which appends one JSON line to a local spool file and exits 0. No network, no daemon, nothing parsed on the hot path.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingest.</strong> <code>coding.sh ingest</code> (and every read command, before it reads) normalizes spool lines into <a href="/docs/trace-format">coding.sh/trace</a> events, redacts secrets, and writes them to the index and blob store.</li>
    <li><strong>Explore.</strong> List, inspect and search sessions in the terminal or in the local viewer.</li>
    <li><strong>Evaluate.</strong> Turn cases into datasets, run any agent over them, grade the outputs, and compare two runs case by case.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="pages">Pages</h2>
  {
    groups.map((g) => (
      <>
        <h3>{g.label}</h3>
        <ul>
          {g.pages.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <a href={p.path}>{p.label}</a>: {p.summary}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    ))
  }

  <h2 id="help">Help and contributing</h2>
  <p>
    The source is on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>. Bugs and questions go to <a href={ISSUES_URL}>issues</a>. The most useful
    contribution right now is a recorded session from an agent version the adapters haven't seen yet.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
